{"id":"mahabharata-7-170","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":170,"title":"सप्तत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 170 · The Narayana weapon's burning","summary":{"en":"Ashvatthaman's weapon blazes against the Pandavas, burning those who resist it, until Bhima's chariot is surrounded by fire. The Kauravas cheer as the Pandavas fear, and Krishna calls upon them to put down their arms.","kn":"ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮನ ಅಸ್ತ್ರ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಮೇಲೆ ಉರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ; ಎದುರಿಸಿದವರನ್ನು ಸುಡುತ್ತದೆ, ಭೀಮನ ರಥವನ್ನು ಬೆಂಕಿ ಸುತ್ತುತ್ತದೆ. ಕೌರವರು ಹರ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಪಾಂಡವರು ಭಯಪಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಆಯುಧ ಕೆಳಗಿಡಲು ಕರೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अश्वत्थामा का अस्त्र पाण्डवों पर जलता है और प्रतिरोध करने वालों को भस्म करता है, भीम के रथ को अग्नि घेर लेती है। कौरव हर्षित और पाण्डव भयभीत होते हैं, और कृष्ण सबको शस्त्र रखने को पुकारते हैं।","te":"అశ్వత్థామ అస్త్రం పాండవులపై మండుతుంది; ఎదిరించినవారిని కాలుస్తుంది, భీముని రథాన్ని అగ్ని చుట్టుముడుతుంది. కౌరవులు సంతోషిస్తారు, పాండవులు భయపడతారు; కృష్ణుడు ఆయుధాలు వదలమని పిలుపునిస్తాడు.","ta":"அஸ்வத்தாமனின் அஸ்திரம் பாண்டவர் மீது எரிந்து எதிர்ப்பவரைச் சுடுகிறது; பீமனின் தேரைத் தீ சூழ்கிறது. கௌரவர் மகிழ, பாண்டவர் அஞ்ச, கண்ணன் ஆயுதம் துறக்கும்படி அழைக்கிறார்.","ml":"അശ്വത്ഥാമാവിന്റെ ആയുധം പാണ്ഡവർക്കെതിരെ ജ്വലിക്കുന്നു; അതിനെ എതിർക്കുന്നവരെ ദഹിപ്പിക്കുന്നു, ഭീമന്റെ രഥം തീകൊണ്ട് വലയം ചെയ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവർ ഭയക്കുമ്പോൾ കൗരവർ ആർത്തുവിളിക്കുന്നു; ആയുധം താഴെവെക്കാൻ കൃഷ്ണൻ അവരെ വിളിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.170; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"नारायणास्त्रमोक्षपर्व","titleEn":"Narayanastramoksha Parva (Release of the Narayana weapon)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः स कदनं चक्रे रिपूणां द्रोणनन्दनः ।\nयुगान्ते सर्वभूतानां कालसृष्ट इवान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son made a slaughter of his enemies, like Death sent by Time at the end of an age to destroy all beings."}},{"n":2,"text":"ध्वजद्रुमं शस्त्रशृङ्गं हतनागमहाशिलम् ।\nअश्वकिंपुरुषाकीर्णं शरासनलतावृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killing his foes with broad arrows, he piled up a mountain of bodies: its trees were banners, its peaks weapons, its great boulders slain elephants, strewn with horses and kimpurushas and covered with creepers of bows,"}},{"n":3,"text":"शूलक्रव्यादसंघुष्टं भूतयक्षगणाकुलम् ।\nनिहत्य शात्रवान्भल्लैः सोऽचिनोद्देहपर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"echoing with spears and the cries of flesh-eaters, and thronged with spirits and yakshas."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो वेगेन महता विनद्य स नरर्षभः ।\nप्रतिज्ञां श्रावयामास पुनरेव तवात्मजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that bull among men roared with great force and again declared his vow to your son."}},{"n":5,"text":"यस्माद्युध्यन्तमाचार्यं धर्मकञ्चुकमास्थितः ।\nमुञ्च शस्त्रमिति प्राह कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, wearing the mantle of dharma, told the fighting teacher \"Lay down your weapon,\""}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्मात्संपश्यतस्तस्य द्रावयिष्यामि वाहिनीम् ।\nविद्राव्य सत्यं हन्तास्मि पापं पाञ्चाल्यमेव तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"therefore, in his sight I shall rout his army; having routed it, I shall surely kill that sinful Panchala."}},{"n":7,"text":"सर्वानेतान्हनिष्यामि यदि योत्स्यन्ति मां रणे ।\nसत्यं ते प्रतिजानामि परावर्तय वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall kill all these if they fight me in battle; I promise you truly. Turn your army back."}},{"n":8,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा तव पुत्रस्तु वाहिनीं पर्यवर्तयत् ।\nसिंहनादेन महता व्यपोह्य सुमहद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing it, your son turned the army back, dispelling its great fear with a mighty lion's roar."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः समागमो राजन्कुरुपाण्डवसेनयोः ।\nपुनरेवाभवत्तीव्रः पूर्णसागरयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, the Kuru and Pandava armies met again fiercely, like two full oceans."}},{"n":10,"text":"संरब्धा हि स्थिरीभूता द्रोणपुत्रेण कौरवाः ।\nउदग्राः पाण्डुपाञ्चाला द्रोणस्य निधनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the Kauravas, steadied by Drona's son, were fired up, and the Pandavas and Panchalas were roused by Drona's death."}},{"n":11,"text":"तेषां परमहृष्टानां जयमात्मनि पश्यताम् ।\nसंरब्धानां महावेगः प्रादुरासीद्रणाजिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they, greatly joyful and eager, saw victory in themselves, a mighty surge arose on the field of battle."}},{"n":12,"text":"यथा शिलोच्चये शैलः सागरे सागरो यथा ।\nप्रतिहन्येत राजेन्द्र तथासन्कुरुपाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a mountain is struck by a mountain, or an ocean by an ocean, O best of kings, so were the Kurus and Pandavas."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः शङ्खसहस्राणि भेरीणामयुतानि च ।\nअवादयन्त संहृष्टाः कुरुपाण्डवसैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then thousands of conches and tens of thousands of drums were sounded gladly by the Kuru and Pandava soldiers."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो निर्मथ्यमानस्य सागरस्येव निस्वनः ।\nअभवत्तस्य सैन्यस्य सुमहानद्भुतोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that army made a great, marvellous roar, like an ocean being churned."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रादुश्चक्रे ततो द्रौणिरस्त्रं नारायणं तदा ।\nअभिसंधाय पाण्डूनां पाञ्चालानां च वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son brought forth the Narayana weapon, aiming it at the army of the Pandavas and Panchalas."}},{"n":16,"text":"प्रादुरासंस्ततो बाणा दीप्ताग्राः खे सहस्रशः ।\nपाण्डवान्भक्षयिष्यन्तो दीप्तास्या इव पन्नगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then arrows appeared in the sky by thousands, fiery-tipped, like blazing-mouthed serpents about to devour the Pandavas."}},{"n":17,"text":"ते दिशः खं च सैन्यं च समावृण्वन्महाहवे ।\nमुहूर्ताद्भास्करस्येव राजँल्लोकं गभस्तयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They covered the directions, the sky and the army in the great battle, as a sun's rays cover the world in a moment, O king."}},{"n":18,"text":"तथापरे द्योतमाना ज्योतींषीवाम्बरेऽमले ।\nप्रादुरासन्महीपाल कार्ष्णायसमया गुडाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others appeared, O king, glowing like stars in a clear sky, balls of black iron."}},{"n":19,"text":"चतुर्दिशं विचित्राश्च शतघ्न्योऽथ हुताशदाः ।\nचक्राणि च क्षुरान्तानि मण्डलानीव भास्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In all four directions appeared strange shataghnis and fire-throwers, and discs edged with razors like the sun's orbs."}},{"n":20,"text":"शस्त्राकृतिभिराकीर्णमतीव भरतर्षभ ।\nदृष्ट्वान्तरिक्षमाविग्नाः पाण्डुपाञ्चालसृञ्जयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sky was thickly strewn with the forms of weapons, bull of the Bharatas, and the Pandavas, Panchalas and Srinjayas were alarmed at the sight."}},{"n":21,"text":"यथा यथा ह्ययुध्यन्त पाण्डवानां महारथाः ।\nतथा तथा तदस्त्रं वै व्यवर्धत जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The more the great chariot-warriors of the Pandavas fought, O lord of men, the more that weapon grew."}},{"n":22,"text":"वध्यमानास्तथास्त्रेण तेन नारायणेन वै ।\nदह्यमानानलेनेव सर्वतोऽभ्यर्दिता रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by that Narayana weapon, they were tormented on every side in the battle as if burned by fire."}},{"n":23,"text":"यथा हि शिशिरापाये दहेत्कक्षं हुताशनः ।\nतथा तदस्त्रं पाण्डूनां ददाह ध्वजिनीं प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"As fire burns dry grass when winter ends, so that weapon burned the Pandava army, lord."}},{"n":24,"text":"आपूर्यमाणेनास्त्रेण सैन्ये क्षीयति चाभिभो ।\nजगाम परमं त्रासं धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the weapon swelled and the army dwindled, O mighty one, Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, fell into great terror."}},{"n":25,"text":"द्रवमाणं तु तत्सैन्यं दृष्ट्वा विगतचेतनम् ।\nमध्यस्थतां च पार्थस्य धर्मपुत्रोऽब्रवीदिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the army fleeing, senseless, and Partha standing neutral, the son of Dharma said this."}},{"n":26,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्न पलायस्व सह पाञ्चालसेनया ।\nसात्यके त्वं च गच्छस्व वृष्ण्यन्धकवृतो गृहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said: Dhrishtadyumna, flee with the Panchala army; and you, Satyaki, go to the homes of the Vrishnis and Andhakas."}},{"n":27,"text":"वासुदेवोऽपि धर्मात्मा करिष्यत्यात्मनः क्षमम् ।\nउपदेष्टुं समर्थोऽयं लोकस्य किमुतात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva too, soul of dharma, will do what is right for himself; he is able to instruct the world, how much more himself."}},{"n":28,"text":"संग्रामस्तु न कर्तव्यः सर्वसैन्यान्ब्रवीमि वः ।\nअहं हि सह सोदर्यैः प्रवेक्ष्ये हव्यवाहनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I tell all the armies: no battle is to be fought. I with my brothers shall enter the fire."}},{"n":29,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणार्णवं तीर्त्वा संग्रामं भीरुदुस्तरम् ।\nअवसत्स्याम्यसलिले सगणो द्रौणिगोष्पदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having crossed the sea of Bhishma and Drona, a battle hard for cowards to cross, I shall stay with my kin in the waterless puddle of Drona's son's hoofprint."}},{"n":30,"text":"कामः संपद्यतामस्य बीभत्सोराशु मां प्रति ।\nकल्याणवृत्त आचार्यो मया युधि निपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let Bibhatsu's wish be quickly fulfilled regarding me: I felled in battle the teacher of good conduct,"}},{"n":31,"text":"येन बालः स सौभद्रो युद्धानामविशारदः ।\nसमर्थैर्बहुभिः क्रूरैर्घातितो नाभिपालितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"through whom the boy Saubhadra, unskilled in war, was killed by many strong, cruel men and not protected."}},{"n":32,"text":"येनाविब्रुवता प्रश्नं तथा कृष्णा सभां गता ।\nउपेक्षिता सपुत्रेण दासभावं नियच्छती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through whom Krishna, who was silent and did not ask a question, went into the assembly and was ignored, together with her sons, as she was subjected to slavery."}},{"n":33,"text":"जिघांसुर्धार्तराष्ट्रश्च श्रान्तेष्वश्वेषु फल्गुनम् ।\nकवचेन तथा युक्तो रक्षार्थं सैन्धवस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Dhritarashtra's son wished to kill Phalguna while his horses were tired, he was armed in armour for the protection of the Sindhu king."}},{"n":34,"text":"येन ब्रह्मास्त्रविदुषा पाञ्चालाः सत्यजिन्मुखाः ।\nकुर्वाणा मज्जये यत्नं समूला विनिपातिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By him, a knower of the brahma weapon, the Panchalas headed by Satyajit were destroyed root and all as they tried to save him."}},{"n":35,"text":"येन प्रव्राज्यमानाश्च राज्याद्वयमधर्मतः ।\nनिवार्यमाणेनास्माभिरनुगन्तुं तदेषिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By him, when we were being sent from the kingdom unrighteously and tried to follow, we were kept from it."}},{"n":36,"text":"योऽसावत्यन्तमस्मासु कुर्वाणः सौहृदं परम् ।\nहतस्तदर्थे मरणं गमिष्यामि सबान्धवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who always showed us the highest friendship has been killed for it; I shall go to death with my kin."}},{"n":37,"text":"एवं ब्रुवति कौन्तेये दाशार्हस्त्वरितस्ततः ।\nनिवार्य सैन्यं बाहुभ्यामिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the son of Kunti spoke thus, Dasharha hurriedly stopped the army with both arms and said these words."}},{"n":38,"text":"शीघ्रं न्यस्यत शस्त्राणि वाहेभ्यश्चावरोहत ।\nएष योगोऽत्र विहितः प्रतिघातो महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: Quickly lay down your weapons and get down from your mounts. This is the means that the great being has devised against it."}},{"n":39,"text":"द्विपाश्वस्यन्दनेभ्यश्च क्षितिं सर्वेऽवरोहत ।\nएवमेतन्न वो हन्यादस्त्रं भूमौ निरायुधान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Get down to the ground from elephants, horses and chariots, all of you. In this way the weapon will not strike you if you stand unarmed on the ground."}},{"n":40,"text":"यथा यथा हि युध्यन्ते योधा ह्यस्त्रबलं प्रति ।\nतथा तथा भवन्त्येते कौरवा बलवत्तराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the more the warriors fight against the force of the weapon, the stronger these Kauravas become."}},{"n":41,"text":"निक्षेप्स्यन्ति च शस्त्राणि वाहनेभ्योऽवरुह्य ये ।\nतान्नैतदस्त्रं संग्रामे निहनिष्यति मानवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who throw down their weapons, getting down from their mounts, this weapon will not kill them in battle."}},{"n":42,"text":"ये त्वेतत्प्रतियोत्स्यन्ति मनसापीह केचन ।\nनिहनिष्यति तान्सर्वान्रसातलगतानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But any who try to resist it, even only in thought, it will kill all of them even if they go down to the nether world."}},{"n":43,"text":"ते वचस्तस्य तच्छ्रुत्वा वासुदेवस्य भारत ।\nईषुः सर्वेऽस्त्रमुत्स्रष्टुं मनोभिः करणेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that word of Vasudeva, O Bharata, they all wished to throw down the weapon, in mind and in act."}},{"n":44,"text":"तत उत्स्रष्टुकामांस्तानस्त्राण्यालक्ष्य पाण्डवः ।\nभीमसेनोऽब्रवीद्राजन्निदं संहर्षयन्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them about to throw down the weapons, Bhimasena the Pandava, O king, spoke these words to cheer them."}},{"n":45,"text":"न कथंचन शस्त्राणि मोक्तव्यानीह केनचित् ।\nअहमावारयिष्यामि द्रोणपुत्रास्त्रमाशुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said: By no means should anyone here let go of weapons. I shall check the weapon of Drona's son with my arrows."}},{"n":46,"text":"अथ वाप्यनया गुर्व्या हेमविग्रहया रणे ।\nकालवद्विचरिष्यामि द्रौणेरस्त्रं विशातयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or else with this heavy golden mace I shall move in battle like Time itself, shattering the weapon of Drona's son."}},{"n":47,"text":"न हि मे विक्रमे तुल्यः कश्चिदस्ति पुमानिह ।\nयथैव सवितुस्तुल्यं ज्योतिरन्यन्न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"No man here is my equal in prowess, just as there is no other light equal to the sun."}},{"n":48,"text":"पश्यध्वं मे दृढौ बाहू नागराजकरोपमा ।\nसमर्थौ पर्वतस्यापि शैशिरस्य निपातने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at my firm arms, like the trunks of king-elephants, able to fell even a snowy mountain."}},{"n":49,"text":"नागायुतसमप्राणो ह्यहमेको नरेष्विह ।\nशक्रो यथा प्रतिद्वंद्वो दिवि देवेषु विश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among men I alone have the strength of ten thousand elephants, as Shakra among the gods is renowned in heaven as having no rival."}},{"n":50,"text":"अद्य पश्यत मे वीर्यं बाह्वोः पीनांसयोर्युधि ।\nज्वलमानस्य दीप्तस्य द्रौणेरस्त्रस्य वारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today watch the power in my arms, with their solid shoulders, in battle as I stop the blazing, flaming weapon of Drona's son."}},{"n":51,"text":"यदि नारायणास्त्रस्य प्रतियोद्धा न विद्यते ।\nअद्यैनं प्रतियोत्स्यामि पश्यत्सु कुरुपाण्डुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"If there is none to oppose the Narayana weapon, today I shall oppose it while the Kurus and Pandavas look on."}},{"n":52,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो भीमो द्रोणपुत्रमरिंदमः ।\nअभ्ययान्मेघघोषेण रथेनादित्यवर्चसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said so, Bhima, scourge of enemies, went toward Drona's son in a chariot rumbling like a cloud and radiant as the sun."}},{"n":53,"text":"स एनमिषुजालेन लघुत्वाच्छीघ्रविक्रमः ।\nनिमेषमात्रेणासाद्य कुन्तीपुत्रोऽभ्यवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That son of Kunti, swift in attack, reached him in a moment because of his lightness of hand and covered him with a net of arrows."}},{"n":54,"text":"ततो द्रौणिः प्रहस्यैनमुदासमभिभाष्य च ।\nअवाकिरत्प्रदीप्ताग्रैः शरैस्तैरभिमन्त्रितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son, laughing and speaking to him with indifference, covered him with those fire-tipped arrows, empowered by mantras."}},{"n":55,"text":"पन्नगैरिव दीप्तास्यैर्वमद्भिरनलं रणे ।\nअवकीर्णोऽभवत्पार्थः स्फुलिङ्गैरिव काञ्चनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by the arrows, like blazing-mouthed serpents spitting fire in battle, Partha was covered as if with golden sparks."}},{"n":56,"text":"तस्य रूपमभूद्राजन्भीमसेनस्य संयुगे ।\nखद्योतैरावृतस्येव पर्वतस्य दिनक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, Bhimasena's appearance in the battle was like a mountain at the close of day covered with fireflies."}},{"n":57,"text":"तदस्त्रं द्रोणपुत्रस्य तस्मिन्प्रतिसमस्यति ।\nअवर्धत महाराज यथाग्निरनिलोद्धतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he opposed it, that weapon of Drona's son grew, O great king, as a fire fanned by the wind."}},{"n":58,"text":"विवर्धमानमालक्ष्य तदस्त्रं भीमविक्रमम् ।\nपाण्डुसैन्यमृते भीमं सुमहद्भयमाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that weapon growing against Bhima's valour, a very great fear entered the Pandava army, except Bhima."}},{"n":59,"text":"ततः शस्त्राणि ते सर्वे समुत्सृज्य महीतले ।\nअवारोहन्रथेभ्यश्च हस्त्यश्वेभ्यश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they all cast their weapons to the ground and got down from their chariots, elephants and horses everywhere."}},{"n":60,"text":"तेषु निक्षिप्तशस्त्रेषु वाहनेभ्यश्च्युतेषु च ।\nतदस्त्रवीर्यं विपुलं भीममूर्धन्यथापतत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they had thrown down their weapons and descended from their mounts, the vast power of that weapon fell upon Bhima's head."}},{"n":61,"text":"हाहाकृतानि भूतानि पाण्डवाश्च विशेषतः ।\nभीमसेनमपश्यन्त तेजसा संवृतं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beings cried out \"Alas!\", and the Pandavas especially, seeing Bhimasena then enveloped in its blaze."}}]}]}